<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:42Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>No, this video doesn't disprove the 9/11 attack on the south tower of the World Trade Center</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af91b93732d3ef6c9acae50ef1f7d1ece25c336680f656b0ff5baa46c8a63440</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:01:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11--3315503e2a84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11" /><summary type="html">A former British member of parliament implied that a video filmed from a helicopter on September 11, 2001 shows that no planes actually hit the World Trade Center's south tower, but this claim would be unfounded. The plane that hit the south tower hit the other side of the building, which isn’t visible in the video.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky accuses Putin of using nationals of 47 countries to fight Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9380552302f4bc700c90e2421a46b4d572a6d73496039f6db315ddcd80175b8f</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:53:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-putin-using-citizens-from-47-countries-to-fight-ukraine-zelensky-tells-un--ae57344b771c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-putin-using-citizens-from-47-countries-to-fight-ukraine-zelensky-tells-un" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky told the UN General Assembly on Wednesday that Russian President Vladimir Putin had enlisted fighters from 47 countries including North Korea, Ghana and India to fight against Ukraine. Zelensky also warned that his forces could target Russian heating and energy facilities in the winter months if Moscow continues to attack Ukraine's energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Holy regulation? Pope in Paris to press case for 'disarming' AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3fa6f8798630e31723bc2ff31f0ba9ee4142eeb2329e0be84a325d31e740de7</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:44:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260923-holy-regulation-pope-in-paris-to-press-case-for-disarming-ai--69cec545769d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260923-holy-regulation-pope-in-paris-to-press-case-for-disarming-ai" /><summary type="html">It's all about his high holiness here in France. For weeks already, the nation's been abuzz over the upcoming visit of Leo. From Friday evening mass at Notre Dame Cathedral and mass before 600-thousand faithful in Paris to the pilgrimage city of Lourdes and a trip to Metz, hometown of father of European unity Robert Schuman. A papal visit to France usually draws much attention to the symbiotic love-hate relationship between the church and a secular state of mostly-lapsed Catholics. And yes, there have been grumblings about the visit's cost to taxpayers. But the pushback's relatively muted. This new American pope seems genuinely popular here in France. We'll ask why.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'Breakthrough' archeological find could confirm location of Paris's original settlement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94925ab2e1df177936eaef42aaf8bb2f59fa64b46136596f5732268b0d392938</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:19:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-breakthrough-archeological-find-could-confirm-paris-origins--3ef95495d245.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-breakthrough-archeological-find-could-confirm-paris-origins" /><summary type="html">An ancient wall discovered this summer under a hospital in central Paris is thought to be a fragment of city ramparts built by Iron age settlers. Experts say the stone-and-wood structure could confirm the location of the ancient city of Lutetia.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: 'Russia will never stop,' Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d53378602a81cb771ef8fa4614f1fcee7e409ccb4f4239f185eb921adc0912f1</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:05:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war--40872fea338b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Harvey Weinstein sentenced to 15 years in prison for 2006 sex assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fab3fabeb1603f8e816c033c60746bff18ab44268702e614555c256427eb993b</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:56:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault--91ffc4aa930f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault" /></entry><entry><title>Disgraced Hollywood mogul Harvey Weinstein sentenced to 15 years for 2006 sex assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2215cbfb17d6db4167d56840fc4b3e147de763405785264aa7c5ba68bc9592c3</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:55:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault--91ffc4aa930f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault" /><summary type="html">Disgraced movie mogul Harvey Weinstein was sentenced to 15 years in prison Wednesday in another #MeToo reckoning for sexually assaulting a former production assistant in 2006.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Iran will 'never bend at the knee', Pezeshkian tells UN in defiant wartime address</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2edf028b250d5e3cddb0b8e8a814ea04a41362510b0a4acbfac1c72496ff7740</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:49:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address--10f22d78db02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian gave a defiant wartime address at the UN on Wednesday accusing the US of terrorism in his country and saying Iran would not "bend at the knee". But as Pezeshkian called for diplomacy, Iranian officials downplayed their talks with US counterparts on the sidelines of the gerenal assembly as "not anything new".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash against smart glasses grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc35ce118b1ec7872f1c47bad69a930bcfce5414c7ba408d2a0fc92f95cd7e40</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:30:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/backlash-against-smart-glasses-grow--239c47ee68f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/backlash-against-smart-glasses-grow" /><summary type="html">Paris prosecutors say they have opened several investigations after receiving complaints about women allegedly filmed on the street without their consent by people wearing so-called “smart glasses”. Calls are growing across Europe for action against what campaigners have dubbed “pervert” smart glasses, after secretly filmed footage of women and girls appeared online. Solange Mougin reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US says wants Ukraine, Russia to end strikes on energy sites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:562e0123fe737500e09bbfdcf75dd86ec06f88a5b306dacc194fa65be632abd8</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:25:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1--6a47cb7c5c74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is due to address the UN General Assembly on Wednesday, as US President Donald Trump pushes for an end to Russia’s war and Kyiv seeks to shape renewed diplomatic efforts after more than four and a half years of conflict. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy set to address UN as Russia strikes Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e07197c334a6e8cb3d9e674c7be2623f6746069909d3b651e1ae9cda1bc1308f</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:20:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1--602f8dc2d515.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1" /><summary type="html">Russia hammered Ukraine’s capital, Kyiv, with drones in daylight attacks on Wednesday, killing two people and wounding 23, just hours before Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy was due to address world leaders at the UN General Assembly. Zelenskyy met US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, as Trump has expressed frustration over the lack of progress in talks aimed at ending the war and the continued escalation of aerial attacks by both sides. Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iranian president adresses UNGA amid war with US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85ee5728ec376843125d5af1049869ebfc5200154b5ee05aee17956f88d8ce27</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:20:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iranian-president-adresses-unga-amid-war-with-us--55dbecdb0c30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iranian-president-adresses-unga-amid-war-with-us" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".  France 24 correspondent from New York, Jessica Le Masurier, tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why is France's Gen Z turning to Catholicism?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f890671fa317a94c0afb19885bd940d72491057258cf0ccbc331aaf8c02d2a25</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:18:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20260923-why-is-france-s-gen-z-turning-to-catholicism--6e00a6b91560.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20260923-why-is-france-s-gen-z-turning-to-catholicism" /><summary type="html">As France prepares for Pope Leo XIV's visit, a surprising trend has emerged in recent years: the number of baptisms among teenagers and young adults has skyrocketed. More than 21,000 catechumens, those undergoing the period of preparation for baptism into the Christian Church, have been recorded so far in 2026. How can this renewed interest in the Catholic faith be explained? Florence Gaillard reports for France in Focus.</summary><category term="France in focus" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV to trace back French ancestry, spiritual roots on visit to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2333cea50c26e2383838319344a01430efe2b41824dbfa979039f54e983ecdc</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:02:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-pope-leo-xiv-trace-back-french-ancestry-spiritual-roots-visit-to-france--c0e27df6d9b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-pope-leo-xiv-trace-back-french-ancestry-spiritual-roots-visit-to-france" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo’s four-day visit to France, which kicks off on Friday, is something of a homecoming for the Chicago-born pontiff, a grandson of European immigrants with family roots in Normandy. His spiritual roots in French Catholicism run deeper still.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino: Climate scientists warn of "Godzilla-level" climate event</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f3c58d26fdfc5ee2a767ec202390d20675e7675d793ad9dec8887a1c06ca4d1</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:59:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-el-nino-climate-scientists-warn-of-godzilla-level-climate-event--958c99d6c419.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-el-nino-climate-scientists-warn-of-godzilla-level-climate-event" /><summary type="html">Extreme heat caused by this year’s “super El Niño” could lead to as many as 451,000 excess deaths worldwide in the six months to February 2027, according to researchers at the University of Chicago’s Climate Impact Lab. The number of extremely hot days is expected to rise by 44%, with Nigeria, Indonesia and Sudan among the countries likely to be worst affected. Researchers warn that the impact could extend well beyond the six-month period studied. Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:090d4f8555b68a84bea71bbe1ef51031647e7b844f0ee333154dcde7960beeff</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism--68195566b037.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Iranian President Pezeshkian adresses UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4270750c616fb37a916f8aee7462094c456cf9c1756c8bfa7c6350a033174472</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:44:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1--ba655932baa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Watch live: Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de5c723469b9db8fa18d9b124ee45a83c242a909b661ce75ac4547083e8985ab</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:30:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war--40872fea338b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war" /></entry><entry><title>Film show: Brad Pitt and his dog take on the wilderness in 'Heart of the Beast'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c55f26602e3454f47d817904ccc8ec6581bb9776d8c656630542e35404a433f8</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:48:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260923-film-show-brad-pitt-and-his-dog-take-on-the-wilderness-in-heart-of-the-beast--dfe8bff7d7e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260923-film-show-brad-pitt-and-his-dog-take-on-the-wilderness-in-heart-of-the-beast" /><summary type="html">Eve Jackson and film critic Emma Jones run through this week's new cinema releases in France. Brad Pitt heads into the Alaskan wilderness with his four-legged co-star in "Heart of the Beast". Also, Robert Pattinson takes on a controversial TV host in "Primetime", a new generation discovers "Sense and Sensibility", and Julia Donaldson and Axel Scheffler's "The Scarecrows' Wedding" arrives on the big screen.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Super El Niño could cause 451,000 excess deaths worldwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13fe1ec39d25d878be2e1039579e9526bfbdd46bfc8d105d81d4dded866e1127</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:37:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-super-el-ni_o-could-cause-451-000-excess-deaths-worldwide--34dfb744a8fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-super-el-ni%C3%B1o-could-cause-451-000-excess-deaths-worldwide" /><summary type="html">Extreme heat linked to this year’s “super El Niño” could cause up to 451,000 excess deaths worldwide in the six months to February 2027, according to researchers at the University of Chicago’s Climate Impact Lab. The number of extremely hot days is expected to rise by 44%, with Nigeria, Indonesia and Sudan among the countries likely to be most affected. Researchers warn that the impact could extend well beyond the six-month period studied. Chloe Brimicombe, a climate scientist from the University of Oxford, shares further details about this climate phenomenon.</summary></entry><entry><title>How US players are reshaping France and the continent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbe2853219d2208aa0826b972081340a6ab348163ba0e79da2800eacaf6331bf</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:33:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260923-how-us-players-are-reshaping-france-and-the-continent--e00e75333f5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260923-how-us-players-are-reshaping-france-and-the-continent" /><summary type="html">In this edition we welcome CNN's correspondent in France, Melissa Bell. Melissa is the author of "Sous l'influence americaine", an investigation into American interference in France and Europe. She tells us about the ways in which American interference is being felt in Europe and France and what we should expect during the 2027 French presidential election campaign.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Golan Heights will 'remain Syrian', President Ahmed al-Sharaa vows at UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae2ad0b71512ad7abf6284ccafa674496cf74e614d35d298c4863abaf28c2a00</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:31:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un--f84fe9f69d85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un" /><summary type="html">Syria's President Ahmed al-Sharaa told the UN Wednesday that the contested Golan Heights region would "remain Syrian" despite ongoing military occupation by Israel. The Syrian leader also used his second turn at the UN rostrum to denounce repeated Israeli strikes on his country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Six-year-old girl breaks Rubik's Cube world record</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0468d8bd33991bd53950141022968cbfe171983d9420e992912cf0200a25dd6d</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:26:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-six-year-old-girl-breaks-rubik-s-cube-world-record--0c656c078cc6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-six-year-old-girl-breaks-rubik-s-cube-world-record" /><summary type="html">🥇 Lian Yunzhi broke the women's world record for solving a Rubik's Cube - at just six years old!
 
Here's how she did it ▶️
 
#RubiksCube #WorldRecord</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump ramps up his war on the media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85a33a058508d436580d33eaddbc46305cb549d0df1541f34a4f63a95e175f93</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:25:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-trump-ramps-up-his-war-on-the-media--a04596e230e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-trump-ramps-up-his-war-on-the-media" /><summary type="html">US media outlets CNN, Politico and MS NOW are suing the Trump administration after it removed their press credentials and banned them from covering the White House. FRANCE 24 spoke to Steven Herman, executive director of the Jordan Center for Journalism Advocacy and Innovation at the University of Mississippi about the legality of the move and its wider ramnifications.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry></feed>
